{"t": 102.18, "n": 85, "ev": "result", "ok": true, "text": "I wrote the task table for Phase 7 in `docs/plans/i203a.plan.md`. That was the only phase with no rows. I didn't run any tests, since this step has no shell.\n\n- **Rows:** Phase 7 has rows 7.1 to 7.10, all with empty Completed cells. Nine are test rows and one is a code row, so the code row comes last.\n- **Test rows:**\n  - **Rows 7.1 to 7.3:** `test_regeneration.py`, `test_regeneration_run.py` and `test_regeneration_briefs.py` hold the new finding form and the RGN-AC13, RGN-AC14 and RGN-AC15 ids.\n  - **Row 7.4:** `test_spec_budget_and_moved_ids.py` drops the stamp assertion.\n  - **Rows 7.5 to 7.9:** the five fixtures under `evals/checks/regeneration/` are two must-pass and three must-fail.\n- **Code row:** Row 7.10 changes only `regeneration_check` in `regeneration.py`. It reads the report from the `regeneration_report` artifact, falling back to the fixed path. Every result names `ts-rgn-declaration`, `ts-rgn-ran` or `ts-rgn-passed`.\n- **Design choice in row 7.10:** a plain failure's finding moves its old criterion, the rung or command, into the front of its message. The criterion becomes `ts-rgn-passed`. `findings_of` keeps its form, so `test_regeneration_findings.py` needs no row and rows 4.1 and 4.6 keep their marks.\n- **Unchanged:** I left every other row, its mark and the plan's status alone. The existing proof table already has a row for each AC and its commands are in `tempergraph.commands.json`, so it needed no edit.\n- **ID I chose:** Row 7.4 cites WUP-AC7 for its proof. That criterion lists WUP-B13 among others and is the closest fit, so check it.\n\nARTIFACT phases: docs/plans/i203a.plan.md", "subtype": "success", "is_error": false, "session_id": "29470d26-c6ee-4ae9-97b0-d61158ee6b55"}
